# Line endings
#
# Every text file is stored AND checked out with LF, on Windows too. Without
# this, Git's core.autocrlf setting (on by default on Windows) rewrites files
# to CRLF on checkout, which shows the whole project as modified on one
# machine and not on another. Node, Vite, Vitest and the Arduino IDE all read
# LF files correctly on Windows.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Explicit for the file types in this project, so the rule survives even if
# someone changes the line above.
*.ts   text eol=lf
*.ino  text eol=lf
*.py   text eol=lf
*.html text eol=lf
*.css  text eol=lf
*.json text eol=lf
*.md   text eol=lf
*.yml  text eol=lf

# Never convert these: Git would corrupt them by rewriting bytes that happen
# to look like line endings.
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif  binary
*.webp binary
*.ico  binary
*.svg  text eol=lf
*.woff  binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf  binary
*.otf  binary
*.pdf  binary
*.zip  binary

# Keep the generated lockfile out of diffs and merge noise.
package-lock.json -diff linguist-generated

# GitHub language stats: this is a TypeScript project that ships Arduino
# teaching sketches, so do not let the .ino files dominate the language bar.
src/examples/*.ino linguist-documentation
src/examples/python/*.py linguist-documentation

# Intel HEX test fixtures: keep exact bytes (some have CRLF on purpose).
tests/fixtures/upload/*.hex binary
